<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! realm.epoch.rolls ~ roll ~ a new hosting epoch

`lares host roll` lands a new signed hosting act on this hearth's hosting doc in the Nexus (`--nexus <aid>`, else this hearth's own charter); every grant and token two epochs back dies, and rolling twice ends the previous epoch too: the hard roll. `--cap <n>` sets the invites per lineage per epoch. A hearth hosts only as one face: the face that holds its hosting there, else at the first roll `--face N`, else the one face standing open. The walker route ships shut by name, so no gate seats a walker on the epoch until a live grant reader opens it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ roll · capped

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`roll` params=`~ roll the epoch on this hearth's own charter`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`capped` params=`nexus/<aid> cap/5 ~ roll in a Nexus with a cap of five`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ face · nexus · cap

<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/face`>>

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`nexus` params=`takes/aid ~ the Nexus to act in; absent, this hearth's own charter`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`cap` params=`takes/n ~ invites per lineage per epoch, at least 1`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ custody

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`custody` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ one sealed act frame on the custody door under the vessel key; the hosting state never rests in the clear`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · refused · error

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[realm.epoch.rolls cap/5]] ~ --cap names no whole number of at least 1`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`refused` params=`~ the custody door refused the act; the message names why`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`error` params=`~ the act failed outside the door's refusals`>>
```

